1. Install a specialized meter that measures PM, NOx, and CO2 directly;
2. Adjust the catalytic converter settings to reduce emissions;
3. Attach an exhaust manifold to increase flow;
4. Use a vacuum cleaner or a specialized hose to bypass the catalytic converter.

